{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They sacrificed to demons, not El.</b> There is in them no benefit or divine power whatsoever, and they did not know them as divine beings — like the angels on high, the separate Intelligences that were created of old, either before the six days of Creation, or on the second day, or on the fifth day. They are rather 'newcomers, recently come,' that is, newly created beings, recently born; and he says this because they die like human beings and reproduce like human beings — 'of late they came' — they did not reckon them, they neither reckoned nor feared them. Or one may say 'newcomers, recently came': that we learned this matter of novelty recently from the Egyptians, who were expert and practiced in it." "<b>And furthermore,</b> one may interpret יזבחו לשדים — 'they sacrificed to demons' — according to the fact that the types of idolatry are three. The first is the worship of the Intelligences, concerning which we were warned (Exodus 20:3) לא יהיה לך — 'You shall have no [other gods before Me].' The second is the worship of graven images, to draw down spirituality from the stars and constellations into them, concerning which we were warned (ibid.) לא תעשה לך — 'You shall not make for yourself.' And the third is the worship of demons, concerning which we were warned (ibid.) ואשר במים מתחת לארץ — 'and that which is in the waters beneath the earth' — for these are the demons that are in the abyss. Therefore He now warns concerning this third type and says, יזבחו לשדים. And He says לא אלוה — 'not a god' — because there is in them no divine power and dominion like that of the stars and constellations, which are above them. And He says אלהים לא ידעום — 'gods they did not know' — that is, it goes without saying that there is in them no divine power, which is the first Power, for they did not know them and their apprehension did not extend to that; rather, they are 'newcomers, recently come'; 'of late' — your fathers did not reckon them. These are Terah and Nahor, who were worshippers of graven images, to draw down and bring into them the spirituality of the stars and constellations; they did not exert themselves to perform this worship, for their wisdom was not so base. And all this is to distance this worship from them, for they were drawn after it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:18.420031550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}